:: Rowan Sleep
<<set _autosavehere to true>>
<<sleepeffects>><<sleep>><<effects>>
You rest your head on the soft worn bed and manage to fall asleep.
<br><br>
<<if Time.hour gt 22 or Time.hour lt 4>>
    <<npc Rowan>><<person1>>
    You're barely awake when you feel the mattress dip behind you, then an arm sliding around your waist, pulling you back against a warm chest.
    <br><br>
    "Mornin'." <<His>> voice is rough with sleep, mouth pressed against your shoulder. "You got about five more minutes before I gotta drag you out to the field."
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Steal a kiss|Rowan Steal Kiss]]>><</link>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Pretend to sleep|Rowan Pretend Sleep]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Settings [exitCheckBypass]
<<set $settingsExitPassage to "Rowan Room">>
<<settings>>

:: Rowan Passout
<<npc Rowan>><<person1>>
You wake up a few hours later, lying on a warm and soft bed. As your eyes blink open, you see Rowan gently smiling at you. "Mornin' sugar, you alright? Ya must've passed out from all the heat and exhaustion. I'm glad you're startin' to look a bit better."
<br><br>
<<if Time.hour lt 22 and Time.hour gte 4>>
    Rowan sits up and stretches, "I wish I could spare more time but I really gotta get some more workin' in before resting. Try to relax here, okay?"
<<else>>
    Rowan lies next to you, "Take it easy and rest. I'll lay with you."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Bed]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Steal Kiss
You turn over in <<his>> arms and kiss <<him>> before <<he>> can finish waking up properly, and <<he>> makes a low, pleased sound against your mouth, pulling you in closer.
<br><br>
"Mm. Could get used to wakin' up like this." <<He>> tucks a strand of hair behind your ear, looking at you with none of his usual guard up, just soft and unhurried.
<br><br>
Five minutes turns into considerably more than five minutes, and neither of you seems particularly bothered about it.<<arousal 6>><<garousal>><<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Bed]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 5>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Pretend Sleep
You keep your eyes shut, biting back a smile, and let <<him>> think <<he>> hasn't woken you up yet.
<br><br>
"I know you're awake." <<He>> says it right against your ear, far too smug for someone who just got caught. "Your breathin' changed."
<br><br>
"Don't know what you're talking about." You mutter. "Uh huh." <<He>> presses a slow kiss to the back of your shoulder anyway, in no hurry to prove <<his>> point further than that, perfectly content just holding onto you a while longer.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Bed]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 3>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Take Hand
You let <<him>> pull you in, one hand at your waist, the other tangled loosely with yours, and <<he>> moves you both in a slow, unhurried circle that has absolutely nothing to do with skill and everything to do with wanting an excuse to hold you.
<br><br>
"You're a terrible dancer," you murmur against <<his>> shoulder.
<br><br>
"Never said I was good at it." <<His>> chin rests against the top of your head, voice rumbling low in <<his>> chest. "Just said I wasn't gonna let it go to waste."
<br><br>
The song ends. Neither of you stops moving for a while after that.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmland]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 5>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Hard Get
"I'm working," you say.
<br><br>
"Uh huh." <<He>> doesn't drop the hand. "You were swayin' along to it two seconds ago. Don't think I didn't see."
<br><br>
"That was involuntary."
<br><br>
"Sure it was." <<He>> tugs you in anyway, grinning when you don't actually resist all that hard, settling <<his>> hands at your waist like <<he>>'s won something. "C'mon. One song."
<br><br>
You let <<him>> have it. The work can wait.<<arousal 6>><<glove>><<garousal>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmland]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 3>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Porch Lean
You let your shoulder rest against his, the mug warm between your hands.
<br><br>
Rowan goes still for half a second, like <<he>> wasn't quite expecting it, then relaxes into it, an arm settling along the back of the porch swing behind you. Not quite around you. Close enough that it might as well be.
<br><br>
"This alright?" <<He>> asks it lightly, like the answer doesn't matter much either way, but <<he>> doesn't move.
<br><br>
"Yeah." You respond.
<br><br>
<<He>> huffs something that's almost a laugh, almost relieved, and the two of you sit there as the light goes from gold to blue to dark, not saying much else, not needing to.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmland]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 5>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Porch Distance
You keep a careful few inches between you, sipping your drink and watching the fields go dark instead of looking at <<him>>.
<br><br>
Rowan doesn't comment on it, doesn't push closer. <<He>> just settles in beside you, easy as anything, content with however much space you're willing to give.
<br><br>
"You don't gotta talk," <<he>> says after a while, not looking over either. "Just figured the company beats sittin' out here by myself."
<br><br>
There's something almost vulnerable in the admission, buried under <<his>> usual drawl. You don't think <<he>> meant to let that much show.
<br><br>
Neither of you says much else, but <<he>> doesn't leave either, not until the mugs go cold and the stars come out properly.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmland]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 2>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Cooking Steal
While <<his>> attention's on your knife work, you swipe a finger through the sauce simmering behind you and bring it to your mouth before <<he>> can stop you.
<br><br>
"Hey—" <<He>> twists you around by the shoulder, half-scandalized, half-laughing. "That's for the dish, not a snack bar."
<br><br>
"Quality control," you say, entirely unrepentant.
<br><br>
"Quality control." <<He>> repeats it like he's never heard anything so ridiculous, but <<he>>'s grinning now, and <<he>> doesn't let go of your shoulder right away. "And? Verdict?"
<br><br>
"Needs salt."
<br><br>
"It does not need salt." <<He>> says it on reflex, already turning to check anyway, muttering something about smart-mouthed racers under his breath that doesn't sound the least bit annoyed.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmhouse]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 4>><<set $dailyrowanbreakfast to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Cooking Behave
You let <<him>> correct your grip, holding still as <<his>> hand wraps around yours, guiding the knife through a proper dice.
<br><br>
"There. See? Not so hard." <<His>> voice is low near your ear, far closer than the lesson strictly requires.
<br><br>
Neither of you moves to put the distance back. The pot simmers, forgotten for a second, and <<his>> hand stays over yours a beat longer than the knife technique calls for.
<br><br>
"...Rowan."
<br><br>
"Mm?" <<He>> doesn't step back. "Somethin' wrong with the lesson?"
<br><br>
"No." You're not sure what else to say to that, and from the way <<his>> mouth curves, <<he>> knows it.<<arousal 4>><<garousal>><<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmhouse]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 3>><<set $dailyrowanbreakfast to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Spending Time Rowan
<<npc Rowan>><<person1>>
The rain's been coming down since dawn, hard enough that training's cancelled and the whole farm has slowed to a crawl.
<br><br>
You find Rowan sprawled on the old couch in the den, one arm slung over the back of it, looking entirely too comfortable for someone usually allergic to sitting still.
<br><br>
"C'mere. Ain't gonna bite." <<He>> pats the empty space beside <<him>>, the corner of <<his>> mouth tugging upward. "Unless you want me to."
<br><br>
<<link [[Sit close|Rowan Sit Close]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Keep busy|Rowan Keep Busy]]>><</link>>

:: Rowan Sit Close
You drop down next to <<him>>, closer than you probably need to, and <<his>> arm slides from the back of the couch to settle around your shoulders like it was always going to end up there.
<br><br>
"There." <<His>> voice is low, pleased, <<his>> thumb tracing slow idle circles against your arm without seeming to notice <<he>>'s doing it. "Knew you'd come around."
<br><br>
The rain keeps falling outside, and neither of you makes any move to do anything but stay exactly like this, <<his>> breath warm against your hair, <<his>> hand finding yours under the blanket like it belongs there.<<arousal 6>><<garousal>><<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmhouse]]>><<set C.npc.Rowan.love += 4>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Rowan Keep Busy
You busy yourself tidying up the den instead, very pointedly not looking at the open space on the couch.
<br><br>
Rowan watches you avoid <<him>> with open amusement. "Ya gonna dust a hole straight through that shelf if you keep that up."
<br><br>
"Just being productive."
<br><br>
"Uh huh." <<He>> doesn't call you on it any further than that, just stretches out, perfectly content to watch you fuss around the room, that lazy, knowing smile never quite leaving <<his>> face.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmhouse]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Fence Mending - Help
You work alongside <<him>>, passing nails, holding boards steady while <<he>> hammers them into place.
<br><br>
Somewhere in the middle of it <<he>> catches your hand instead of the nail you're holding out, pulling you in for a quick, sweat-salted kiss before going right back to work like nothing happened.
<br><br>
"Needed that," <<he>> says simply, already reaching for the next board.<<gglove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmstead]]>><<npcincr "Rowan" love 4>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Fence Mending - Watch
You settle onto a nearby hay bale and watch <<him>> work instead, perfectly content just to observe.
<br><br>
Rowan glances over more than once, clearly aware of the audience, putting just a little more effort into looking capable than the task strictly requires.
<br><br>
"You just gonna sit there and ogle me all afternoon?"
<br><br>
"Pretty much, yeah."
<br><br>
<<He>> laughs, shaking <<his>> head, but <<he>> doesn't seem to mind one bit.<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmstead]]>><<npcincr "Rowan" love 4>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: TF Recognition - Notices
Rowan stops dead a few feet away, staring at you with an expression caught somewhere between confusion and dawning alarm.
<br><br>
"...Darlin'?" <<His>> eyes flick upward, searching for something that isn't there anymore. "Where'd your horse ears go?"
<br><br>
<<He>> closes the distance fast, hands coming up to your face, tilting your head this way and that like <<he>>'s checking for a fever, or possibly for a prank.
<br><br>
"This some kinda joke? 'Cause it's not funny. Where's the tail, where're the—" <<He>> cuts <<himself>> off, jaw tightening as it visibly sinks in that this isn't a costume malfunction.
<br><br>
<<link [[Reassure Him It's Really You|TF Recognition - Reassure]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Panic Along With Him|TF Recognition - Panic]]>><</link>>

:: TF Recognition - Reassure
"It's really me. I don't know what happened either." You say, reassuring <<him>>.
<br><br>
<<He>> exhales hard, some of the surprise draining out of <<his>> shoulders now that <<he>>'s sure, at least, that you're you. <<His>> hands don't leave your face.
<br><br>
"Okay. Okay." <<He>> says it like <<he>>'s convincing <<himself>>. "You're still you, after all—" <<His>> thumb brushes your cheek, smiling. "My precious star. I got you. Whatever this new era of yours this is."<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmstead]]>><<endevent>><<npcincr "Rowan" love 5>><<set $rowanrecognize to 1>><</link>>

:: TF Recognition - Panic
"I don't know! I just looked down and… and my horse features were gone!" You squeak.
<br><br>
"Okay, okay, nobody panic. Well—" <<He>> gestures vaguely at the obvious panicking happening on both ends. "Too late for that, but—"
<br><br>
<<He>> paces a tight circle, hands laced behind <<his>> head, before stopping abruptly and pulling you into a fierce hug instead, like physically confirming you're still there helps more than thinking does.
<br><br>
"There's stranger things in this world, no? No matter which form you take, you're still my beloved, you got that?"<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Farmstead]]>><<endevent>><<npcincr "Rowan" love 4>><<set $rowanrecognize to 1>><</link>>

:: Talk - Reversed Roles
"You ever think about what if our roles were reversed?" Rowan mutters.
<br><br>
<<He>> chuckles. "I'd make a lousy horse."
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask Why|Reversed Roles - Why]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Agree|Reversed Roles - Agree]]>><</link>>

:: Reversed Roles - Why
"Why's that?"
<br><br>
"Stubborn as a mule, terrible at takin' orders." <<He>> counts it off on <<his>> fingers, grinning. "I'd get myself disqualified the first lap just for sassin' the judges."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Reversed Roles - Agree
"Yeah, probably."
<br><br>
"Hey now." <<He>> looks almost offended, though the grin gives <<him>> away. "Didn't need you agreein' that fast."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Talk - About Alex
"I've heard about another young farmer close to my age around here. Good people, let me tell ya."
<br><br>
<<if $hasMetAlex>>
	You nod, realizing <<he>> must mean Alex.
   <br><br>
	"Small world," you say.
   <br><br>
	"Ain't it just." Rowan looks pleased you already know who <<he>>'s talking about. "<<He>> ever give you grief about your trainer? I got a reputation to live down apparently."<br>
<<else>>
	"Don't think I've met the other farmer," you say.
   <br><br>
	"You will eventually. Can't avoid runnin' into everybody forever, not in a place this small." <<He>> shrugs, already moving on to something else.
   <br>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Talk - Opinion on Mint Mocha
"That stubborn horse, Mint Mocha. Got more attitude than sense, I swear." Rowan shakes <<his>> head, though there's no real venom in it. "Reminds me of myself at that age, if I'm honest. Didn't make me like losin' to them any easier, though."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Talk - Favorite Season
"Ask me, autumn's the best time on a farm. Air gets crisp, work slows down some." <<He>> tilts <<his>> head back, looking at the sky like <<he>>'s picturing it already. "What about you? Got a favorite?"
<br><br>
<<link [[Tell Him Your Favorite|Favorite Season - Answer]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask Him to Guess|Favorite Season - Guess]]>><</link>>

:: Favorite Season - Answer
You tell <<him>>.
<br><br>
"Huh." <<He>> considers it, nodding slowly. "Yeah, I can see that. Suits you, actually."<<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><<npcincr "Rowan" love 1>><</link>>

:: Favorite Season - Guess
"Go on, guess." You say.
<br><br>
Rowan squints at you, studying your face like the answer's written somewhere on it. "...Spring. Somethin' about you seems like a spring person."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks far too pleased with <<himself>>, whether <<he>>'s right or not.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Talk - Compliment Fishing
"So." Rowan leans against the fence post, arms crossed, a little too casual. "How am I doin'? As a trainer, I mean."
<br><br>
<<link [[Genuine Compliment|Compliment Fishing - Genuine]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tease Him|Compliment Fishing - Tease]]>><</link>>

:: Compliment Fishing - Genuine
"Honestly? Pretty good." You respond.
<br><br>
Rowan goes a little still, like <<he>> wasn't fully expecting a straight answer. Then <<he>> clears <<his>> throat, ears faintly pink.
<br><br>
"...Yeah, well. Good to hear." <<He>> looks away first, suddenly very interested in the fence post.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><<npcincr "Rowan" love 3>><</link>>

:: Compliment Fishing - Tease
"Eh. Six out of ten." You say.
<br><br>
"Six?!" <<He>> looks genuinely scandalized. "After everything I've—six?"
<br><br>
"Maybe a seven if you stop fishing for compliments." You respond dryly.
<br><br>
<<He>> huffs, but <<he>>'s fighting a smile the whole time <<he>> pretends to sulk about it.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><<npcincr "Rowan" love 2>><</link>>

:: Talk - Future Plans
"Sometimes I think about what comes after all this. The farm, the races." Rowan's gaze drifts toward the horizon, uncharacteristically distant. "Never get too far in that thought before somethin' drags me back to the present, though."
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask What He'd Want|Future Plans - Ask]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Let It Go|Future Plans - Let Go]]>><</link>>

:: Future Plans - Ask
"What would you want? If you got there." You ask.
<br><br>
Rowan's quiet for a moment, actually thinking about it instead of deflecting with a joke.
<br><br>
"...Somethin' steady, I guess. Somebody to share it with." <<He>> glances at you sideways, then quickly away, clearing <<his>> throat. "Forget I said that."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Rowan Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Future Plans - Let Go
You don't push. Some thoughts seem like they're not finished cooking yet.
<br><br>
Rowan seems grateful for that, giving you a small, appreciative nod before shaking <<himself>> out of it. "Anyway. Back to work."
<br><br>
